## Project layout

- `{{ django_project_slug }}/` — Django settings, URL root, WSGI/ASGI entry points{% if include_celery %}, and the Celery app{% endif %}.
- `apps/{{ initial_app_name }}/` — the first Django app: models, serializers, views, urls,
  tests. New apps follow the same `apps/<name>/` layout and are added to `INSTALLED_APPS`
  as `apps.<name>`.
- Database: **{{ database }}**{% if database == 'postgres' %}, started via `docker-compose.yml`
  (`docker compose up -d db`) using the devcontainer's own isolated Docker-in-Docker daemon.
  `DATABASE_URL` in `.env` (copy it from `.env.example`) points Django at it{% endif %}.
{% if include_celery %}
- Background tasks run through Celery, with Redis as broker/result backend (also in
  `docker-compose.yml`, `docker compose up -d redis`).
{% endif %}

## Running things

- `uv run python manage.py runserver` — dev server.
- `uv run python manage.py makemigrations` / `migrate` — schema changes.
- `uv run pytest` — test suite (uses SQLite automatically unless `DATABASE_URL` is set, so it
  runs without any external service).
{% if database == 'postgres' or include_celery %}
- `docker compose up -d` — start the local services this project depends on
  ({% if database == 'postgres' %}Postgres{% endif %}{% if database == 'postgres' and include_celery %}, {% endif %}{% if include_celery %}Redis{% endif %}).
{% endif %}
